---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Accessibility | Fusion 360 Generators">
  <h1 class="text-4xl text-ink">Accessibility</h1>
  <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl">
    This site aims to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2
    at level AA. Everyone should be able to find and use the add-ins listed
    here.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl text-ink">What we do</h2>
  <ul class="mt-3 max-w-2xl list-disc space-y-1 pl-6">
    <li>
      Every page can be used with a keyboard alone, with a visible focus
      outline.
    </li>
    <li>Text and controls are checked for colour contrast.</li>
    <li>
      Headings, landmarks and labels are set up for screen readers, and search
      and filter results are announced.
    </li>
    <li>The layout adapts to small screens and to zoom up to 400%.</li>
    <li>Moving content respects the "reduce motion" setting of your device.</li>
    <li>
      The catalogue can be shown as a grid, a carousel or a list, so you can
      pick whichever is easiest for you.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl text-ink">Known limits</h2>
  <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl">
    The site has been checked with automated tools and by keyboard. It has not
    yet been tested by people using screen readers. This page will be updated
    when it has.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl text-ink">Tell us about a problem</h2>
  <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl">
    If something on this site is hard to use, email
    <a href="mailto:fusion360@richardmcquiston.com">
      fusion360@richardmcquiston.com
    </a>
    . Say which page and what you were trying to do, and we will work on it.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl">
    You can also use the{' '}
    <a class="underline" href="/contact/">
      Contact Us
    </a>
    page.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
